        "content": "<p>fitzgen opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14412\">PR #14412</a> from <code>fitzgen:use-same-vmctx-analysis</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This allows GVN to deduplicate the callee <code>vmctx</code> loads for multiple calls into<br>\nimported functions from the same instance.</p>\n<p>This shaves off another ~10% of time from the increment-each-byte compile-time<br>\nbuiltins benchmark.</p>\n<p>There is still some store-to-load forwarding that I would have expected this to unlock that is not happening, which if it did happen I'd expect to see that 10% number jump up to maybe 25% or 50%. Seems related to Cranelift's alias analysis tho, not related to anything here, so I wouldn't delay this PR on that ongoing investigation.</p>\n</blockquote>",
